---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import mealBowl from '../assets/meal-bowl.jpg';
---

<section class="system" id="app">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="kicker">The system</span>
    <h2 style="max-width:15ch"
      >Coaching is the heart. The app is the hands.</h2
    >
    <p class="lede"
      >A real app on your home screen, personalized from your intake. It knows
      your ranges and what you actually like to eat, then does the thinking: at
      home, at the restaurant you didn't pick, over your kids' leftovers. Snap
      it, and it's handled.</p
    >

    <div class="collage">
      <div class="mini c-menu rv">
        <div class="m-kicker">Log a meal · four ways</div>
        <div class="modes" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="mode act"
            ><span class="mi">📸</span><span class="ml">Snap</span><span
              class="ms">plate or menu</span
            ></div
          >
          <div class="mode"
            ><span class="mi">✏️</span><span class="ml">Describe</span><span
              class="ms">type it</span
            ></div
          >
          <div class="mode"
            ><span class="mi">🍳</span><span class="ml">My plan</span><span
              class="ms">exact</span
            ></div
          >
          <div class="mode"
            ><span class="mi mi-hash">#</span><span class="ml">Macros</span><span
              class="ms">I know them</span
            ></div
          >
        </div>
        <div class="meal-res">
          <Image
            class="mr-photo"
            src={mealBowl}
            alt="Logged meal photo: chicken meatballs, rice, and Caesar salad on a white plate"
            widths={[320, 480, 640]}
            sizes="(max-width: 880px) 80vw, 360px"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="mr-name">Chicken meatballs, rice &amp; Caesar</div>
          <div class="mr-sub">Recognized from one photo, portions and all</div>
          <div class="mp"
            ><span>480 <small>cal</small></span><span
              >32 <small>P</small></span
            ><span>35 <small>C</small></span><span>24 <small>F</small></span></div
          >
        </div>
        <h3>Snap the plate. Or just say it.</h3>
        <p class="m-desc"
          >Photograph your food and it's recognized and logged. No time for
          photos? Describe it: “leftover mac and cheese and a handful of
          grapes,” done. Eating out? Snap the menu and get dishes ranked to fit
          the room left in your day.</p
        >
      </div>

      <div class="mini c-voice rv">
        <div class="m-kicker">Monday voice note</div>
        <div class="vn">
          <span class="play" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="wave" aria-hidden="true"
            ><i style="height:10px"></i><i style="height:18px"></i><i
              style="height:26px"></i
            ><i style="height:14px"></i><i style="height:30px"></i><i
              style="height:20px"></i
            ><i style="height:8px"></i><i style="height:24px"></i><i
              style="height:16px"></i
            ><i style="height:28px"></i><i style="height:12px"></i><i
              style="height:22px"></i
            ><i style="height:9px"></i><i style="height:19px"></i><i
              style="height:27px"></i
            ><i style="height:13px"></i></span
          >
          <span class="dur">0:58</span>
        </div>
        <p class="vn-meta"
          ><strong>Week 3, from Callie:</strong> this week we anchor protein at
          breakfast. And we let go of weighing in on Fridays.</p
        >
        <h3>Callie in your ears, every Monday.</h3>
        <p class="m-desc"
          >One focus. One skill. One thing to let go. A weekly reset from a
          coach who knows Monday is a fresh start, not a judgment day.</p
        >
      </div>

      <div class="mini c-groc rv">
        <div class="m-kicker">Plan → Groceries</div>
        <div class="g-item done"
          ><span class="box"></span><span>Chicken thighs, 2 lb</span></div
        >
        <div class="g-item done"
          ><span class="box"></span><span>Greek yogurt, full fat</span></div
        >
        <div class="g-item"><span class="box"></span><span>Eggs, 18 ct</span></div>
        <div class="g-item"
          ><span class="box"></span><span>Frozen berries</span></div
        >
        <h3>A week planned around your kitchen.</h3>
        <p class="m-desc"
          >Your intake covers what you love to eat. The app suggests meals and
          recipes that fit your ranges and your tastes, then writes the grocery
          list. And meals you eat on repeat get saved, so logging them takes one
          tap.</p
        >
      </div>

      <div class="mini c-msg rv">
        <div class="m-kicker">Messages · 1:1 with Callie</div>
        <div class="bubble you"
          >Week fell apart. Birthday cake for dinner Tuesday. Do I start over?</div
        >
        <div class="bubble callie"
          ><span class="b-who">Callie</span>You don't start over, you just start
          logging again. One meal today with protein first. That's the whole
          assignment.</div
        >
        <h3>A real answer when the week blows up.</h3>
        <p class="m-desc"
          >1:1 Messages with push notifications, plus the group coaching thread
          where Callie answers all week. All inside the app, nothing extra to
          download, and your phone number stays yours.</p
        >
      </div>

      <div class="mini c-habits rv">
        <div class="m-kicker">Daily rhythm</div>
        <div class="habit done"
          ><span class="ring"></span><span>Water + electrolytes</span></div
        >
        <div class="habit done"
          ><span class="ring"></span><span>Morning sunlight</span></div
        >
        <div class="habit done"
          ><span class="ring"></span><span>Walk or strength</span></div
        >
        <div class="habit"><span class="ring"></span><span>Meals at home</span></div>
        <h3>Habits that fit a nap schedule.</h3>
        <p class="m-desc"
          >Water, walks, sunlight, strength. A checklist that meets your season,
          no gym required.</p
        >
      </div>
    </div>
    <p
      style="text-align:center;margin-top:40px;font-size:15px;color:var(--ink-soft)"
      ><strong style="color:var(--ink)">No App Store download.</strong> Add it to
      your home screen from the link we send. Twenty seconds, and it lives next to
      your camera. And the word members use most for it? Easy.</p
    >
  </div>
</section>
